      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could the body say what goes wrong without this patch? As far as I can see, since aosp/4368055 `vm_iomap_memory()` already bounds a 4KB VMA in kernel pages and maps it from the `vm_slice_off` slice. What\u0027s left is a `start` that isn\u0027t 16KB-aligned, and bounds that are only checked in 16KB pages. \"A native PFN alone cannot describe every valid 4KB resource offset\" doesn\u0027t quite say that, and the last sentence compares against alternatives that aren\u0027t in the patch.\n\nMaybe something like:\n\n```\nvm_iomap_memory() maps a 4KB VMA from the 16KB page that contains start\nand checks its bounds in 16KB pages. When start is not 16KB-aligned, a\n4KB process finds the resource up to 12KB after the offset it expects,\nand a 4KB VMA can map up to 12KB past the end of the resource.\n```",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "001b453effb4c10893ef59109dfa04814c7b5707",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
