      "message": "Thanks, the first paragraph now says what goes wrong with the bounds. Could the second one say it for an unaligned `start` too? I think \u0027so no separate physical-slice mapping loop is needed\u0027 also still refers to the loop of patch set 39, which isn\u0027t in this patch anymore. Maybe something like:\n\n```\nWhen start is not 16KB-aligned, vm_iomap_memory() maps the resource\nfrom the 16KB page that contains start, so a 4KB process finds it up to\n12KB after the offset it expects. No GKI caller needs that layout, so\nrefuse it in 4KB processes with a logged EOPNOTSUPP. Native processes\nretain the existing mapping semantics.\n```",
