      "writtenOn": "2026-11-01T19:09:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like this loop only runs when `start` isn\u0027t 16KB-aligned (after rounding down to 4KB). Otherwise the slice of `start + offset` is `vm_slice_off`, and since aosp/4368055 `remap_pfn_range()` already maps from that slice. aosp/4368011 always passes `PFN_PHYS(pfn)`, so it never gets here.\n\nI couldn\u0027t find an in-tree caller in GKI that reaches it either: open-dice requires page-aligned regions, `snd_pcm_lib_mmap_iomem()` sits behind the PCM mmap refusal of aosp/4393908, and fbdev, STM, MTD and hpet aren\u0027t in `gki_defconfig`. So I think only vendor modules could (`vm_iomap_memory` is in the exynos, imx, lenovo, pixel, qcom and unisoc symbol lists).\n\nDo you have a driver in mind that maps a resource that isn\u0027t 16KB-aligned into 4KB processes? If not, would refusing that case with `p3s_4k_unsupported()` work for you? Then `p3s_vm_iomap_memory()` only needs the byte bounds before `io_remap_pfn_range()`, and the PTEs keep the slices that `vma_slice_offset()` gives. If you do, the loop looks right to me, and `generic_access_phys()` follows it since aosp/4368007.",
