      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the overflow handling here can be simpler. `len + (start \u0026 ~PAGE_MASK_4KB)` can\u0027t exceed `start + len`, which the line above already checks, so this `check_add_overflow()` never fires. And if rounding `len` up wrapped, `aligned_len` would be 0, which the bounds check below rejects anyway.\n\nSince this path only runs for 4KB VMAs, would `PAGE_ALIGN_4KB(len)` from `include/linux/p3s/const.h` work for you instead of `vma_aligned_size()`? Then the new helper and its `\u003clinux/errno.h\u003e` and `\u003clinux/overflow.h\u003e` includes in `include/linux/p3s/vma.h` could go. `p3s_mmap_phys_object()` in aosp/4368011 only runs for 4KB VMAs too.",
